      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114576,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114577,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114578,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>POT arises in the tooth-bearing segments of the jaw and occurs 2&ndash;3&nbsp;times as frequently in the mandible as in the maxilla.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114579,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases are asymptomatic. Some POTs produce marked cortical expansion.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>POT appears as a well-defined radiolucency associated with unerupted teeth, most commonly the mandibular third molar, producing an apparent pericoronal radiolucency. POT may displace and resorb roots of adjacent teeth {32040459}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114580,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The age range is 2&ndash;19&nbsp;years (mean: 11.4&nbsp;years) and there is a slight male predilection {32040459; 32593436; 32981867; 33079412; 33433252}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114581,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "<p >The etiology is unknown. No mutations were identified in 151&nbsp;cancer-associated genes and 42&nbsp;odontogenesis-associated genes in 3&nbsp;POTs studied with next-generation sequencing {29908099}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:19:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114582,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The expression profile of dentinogenesis-associated genes suggests an inhibition of dentine formation. No <em>BRAF</em> p.V600E mutations were found {29908099}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114583,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>POT is a solid, well-circumscribed, sometimes multilobulated, whitish mass. The crown of a tooth may be embedded but is easily detached {24807692}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114584,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>POT comprises loose or myxoid fibrous tissue containing variable numbers of fusiform and stellate fibroblasts and areas with the appearance of cellular odontogenic mesenchyme. The periphery is covered by a single layer of columnar or cuboidal epithelium, with scant superficial layers of stellate reticulum&ndash;like cells partially enclosed by a thin fibrous capsule. Epithelial cords may appear to be within the lesion as a result of lobular infolding. Extracellular concentric mineralized structures within the epithelium have been reported, but there is no evidence of odontoblastic differentiation or mature dentine.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Mesenchymal cells are positive for vimentin, and subepithelial expression of CD34 and CD138 have been demonstrated in several cases. The Ki-67 index is low (&lt;&nbsp;5%). The epithelial component is positive for pancytokeratins (AE1/AE3), CK5, and CK14, whereas CK19 is usually expressed by the columnar cells. Amelogenin, ameloblastin, and DSPP have also been detected. Other markers are variably expressed {24807692; 28390134; 28543986; 29090496; 29908099}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>POT resembles a mesenchymal proliferation very similar to the dental papilla of a developing tooth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114585,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114586,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114587,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a mass of myxoid dental papilla&ndash;like tissue; entire periphery covered by columnar or cuboidal enamel epithelium.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> focal stellate reticulum&ndash;like cells externally; lobular clefted surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114588,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114589,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>POT does not recur after conservative excision {32040459; 32593436; 32981867; 33079412; 33433252}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:31:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]